{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "102", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "\"Oh, darling, you look… comfortable,\" Seraphina said, adjusting the shimmering train of her emerald green ball gown. The fabric rustled like wind chimes.\n\nLeo shrugged, pulling his sweatshirt tighter. \"And you look like you're about to float away. Ready for the annual Starfall Gala?\"\n\n\"Ready as I'll ever be! It's *the* event of the season, Leo. Do you even know what to expect?\" Seraphina’s perfectly applied lipstick gleamed in the hallway light.\n\n\"Sparkly lights, overpriced canapés, and forced small talk with people I barely recognize? Yeah, pretty much. I figured sweats were the appropriate attire.\" Leo grinned, hoisting a reusable grocery bag over his shoulder.\n\nSeraphina gasped dramatically. \"Sweats? At the Starfall Gala? Honestly! You'll be the only one not dressed to the nines.\"\n\n\"I'm prioritizing comfort, Seraphina. Besides, I’m more interested in the stargazing than the social scene.\"\n\n\"But... the gowns! The jewels! The *atmosphere*!\" She gestured wildly with a bejeweled hand.\n\n\"The atmosphere of awkward networking, you mean? I'm good. Look, I brought snacks. And I downloaded a stargazing app. We can find a quiet spot away from the throng.\"\n\nSeraphina sighed, a small smile playing on her lips. \"You’re incorrigible. Fine. But promise you won’t judge my ensemble.\"\n\n\"Never. Though I might ask questions.\"\n\n*  Seraphina smoothed down her gown, a hint of nervousness flickering in her eyes despite her outward confidence.\n*  Leo adjusted his bag, a small, almost imperceptible smile on his face, indicating he was perfectly content with his choice of attire.\n*  They headed towards the gala entrance, an unlikely pair ready to navigate the evening together, despite their vastly different approaches to the event.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.06885108351707458}, {"token": "Oh", "logprob": -0.2613538